(3672299, 511162, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>So, 6.7742 and yet another top 10 finish, what could I possibly offer to improve this one?  I like the idea, and I like the execution, but I am not a very beg fan of your text.  Even still, a very nice score.  I wish that in my inferiority I could offer you more in the form of a critique.  Nice work, as usual.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  So, 6.7742 and yet another top 10 finish, what could I possibly offer to improve this one?  I like the idea, and I like the execution, but I am not a very beg fan of your text.  Even still, a very nice score.  I wish that in my inferiority I could offer you more in the form of a critique.  Nice work, as usual. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2007-05-21 01:48:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3672320, 509567, 52549, '<td valign="top">WOW! What a shot. Congrats on winning the Yellow.</td>', 'WOW! What a shot. Congrats on winning the Yellow.', '2007-05-21 01:51:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3672344, 511309, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Nice focus and also very nice color.  Your point of view illustrates well exactly what your were looking to convey.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I think that the lighting is what cost you the most points here.  Maybe a little fill flash at the bottom of the frame would have helped balance that strong light at the top of the frame.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> In one word, cluttered.  I agree with the other posters that taking some of the goodies out of the refrigerator would have helped out a bit.  As it is, the cleverness of the cans escaping gets lost in the business of the contents.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Comical and very creative, perhaps one of the more creative entries of the challenge.  With a little better lighting and a little less business in the fridge, I think that you''d have pulled a better score.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Nice focus and also very nice color.  Your point of view illustrates well exactly what your were looking to convey. Lighting: I think that the lighting is what cost you the most points here.  Maybe a little fill flash at the bottom of the frame would have helped balance that strong light at the top of the frame. Composition/Content: In one word, cluttered.  I agree with the other posters that taking some of the goodies out of the refrigerator would have helped out a bit.  As it is, the cleverness of the cans escaping gets lost in the business of the contents. My Opinion: Comical and very creative, perhaps one of the more creative entries of the challenge.  With a little better lighting and a little less business in the fridge, I think that you''d have pulled a better score. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2007-05-21 01:55:15.000000', NULL, 0),
