(3672357, 510411, 52549, '<td valign="top">Can''t stop laughing at this. It''s brilliantly funny. Love the "Scratch''n Stiff Edition" ;-D Great job, huge congrats on top 10.</td>', 'Can''t stop laughing at this. It''s brilliantly funny. Love the "Scratch''n Stiff Edition" ;-D Great job, huge congrats on top 10.', '2007-05-21 01:56:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3672382, 510492, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Terrific depth of field use.  I completely disagree with Tygerr.  I think that the shallow depth of field is one of this one''s strengths.  I would like to see just a little deeper depth of field, but I do like the bokeh-esque feel that you created.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Pretty nice, but that large, white area at the top of the frame is very distracting.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Nice rules of thirds use, and that works nicely to pull the eye onto the subject.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I think that this one could have been executed better, but even with that, 4.6 is a bit low.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Terrific depth of field use.  I completely disagree with Tygerr.  I think that the shallow depth of field is one of this one''s strengths.  I would like to see just a little deeper depth of field, but I do like the bokeh-esque feel that you created. Lighting: Pretty nice, but that large, white area at the top of the frame is very distracting. Composition/Content: Nice rules of thirds use, and that works nicely to pull the eye onto the subject. My Opinion: I think that this one could have been executed better, but even with that, 4.6 is a bit low. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2007-05-21 02:00:10.000000', NULL, 0),
